<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ratnagiri</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ratnagiri is a port town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konkan-coast">Konkan coast</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and the headquarters of a district of the same name. The British exiled the last king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thibaw-min">Thibaw</a>, there after the annexation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-burma">Upper Burma</a> in 1885; he lived in a palace in the town until his death in 1916. It is known for Alphonso mangoes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ratnagiri.jpg" alt="Ratnagiri" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aniket Konkar · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thibaw_Palace_in_Ratnagiri_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
